k (LVB), which has been struggling with allegations of poor governance and a mounting bad loan problem, with DBS Bank India, a part of the Development Bank of Singapore. The RBI has also put a cap of Rs25,000 on withdrawal from LVB’s customers’ accounts till Dec. 16.\nThe implosion at LVB did not happen overnight. In fact, the decay had been setting in for a long time.\n\nThe bank was founded in 1926 by a group of businessmen in the southern Indian state of Tamil Nadu with an aim to finance small businesses in the region. With this principle at its core, the bank continued to grow its loan book gradually, posting decent profits and paying a good dividend to its shareholders.\n\nBut between 2008 and 2017, it decided to change its unique strategy and copy what large banks were doing.\n\nAt the time, India’s leading private lenders such as ICICI Bank and Axis Bank were focusing on corporate players to expand their loan books. LVB joined the bandwagon and initially tasted success.\n\nIt clocked speedy growth by giving loans to large corporates. Between 2008 and 2017, LVB’s loan book rose 515% whereas deposits jumped four times.\n\nHowever, the strategy backfired badly when a bunch of the bank’s borrowers became defaulters. This led to a sharp increase in bad loans or non-performing assets (NPAs) on LVB’s books.", "channel_id": "UCW-WMaK5exMNPdsnl3PjN0A", "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCW-WMaK5exMNPdsnl3PjN0A", "duration": 106, "view_count": 20, "age_limit": 0, "webpage_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6yiGfkJVnA0", "categories": ["People & Blogs"], "tags": ["lvb", "lvb issue", "lvb tamil", "lvb bank tamil", "lvb new rules", "lvb rbi", "lvb moratorium", "sbi", "lvb bank rules", "lvb problm", "lvb bank problm tamil", "bank rules", "sbi rules", "dbs bank", "lvb online", "RBI RULES", "rbi new rules"], "playable_in_embed": true, "live_status": "not_live", "media_type": "video", "_format_sort_fields": ["quality", "res", "fps", "hdr:12", "source", "vcod